 "body": "## Wave 1.4 — Telegram Forwarder quarantine (master prompt §1.4)\n\n**Risk:** the suite publicly advertises a ToS-circumvention technique: `tools/ops/telegram_forwarder/README.md:34` — «يتجاوز Restrict Saving Content بتقنية تحميل-إعادة-رفع» — plus the same claim in the root README feature list. Inside the **public** repository of a medical project this is a reputation/legal liability at any external review.\n\n**Reversible quarantine (no history deletion, per §1 Git rules)**\n- `git rm -r tools/ops/telegram_forwarder` — fully recoverable from history and from this branch\n- root README: public feature section removed\n- CHANGELOG / git-sync mentions: historical records + standalone-repo name strings — intentionally untouched\n- standalone `telegram-tools` repo: NOT touched (its data-flow doc = Wave 2.4)\n\n**Human action (owner):** merge to apply the quarantine to the public tip; optionally relocate the tool to a private repo from this branch if still needed.",
